## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/knit.html
- Summary (EN): The Knit node procedurally generates a grid of knitted fabric stitches, arranged in rows and columns, each shaped as a knit or purl stitch. It outputs a height map along with colour, per-stitch id and UV layers for lighting and texturing.
- Résumé (FR) : Génère une grille de mailles de tricot (endroit ou envers) et sort une hauteur accompagnée de la couleur, de l'identifiant par maille et des UV.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets the output size and metadata", "jitter: optional layer driving per-stitch positional jitter", "direction: optional layer orienting each stitch", "angle: optional layer rotating each stitch", "scale: optional layer resizing each stitch", "stretch: optional layer stretching each stitch", "color: optional RGB layer tinting each stitch", "alpha: optional mask layer controlling per-stitch opacity", "flip: optional layer switching stitches between knit and purl"]

- Key parameters: ["Preset: loads predefined knit style settings and overwrites other parameters", "Seed: controls all randomization", "Rows / Columns: size of the stitch grid", "Knit Shape Type: Purl (bumpy) or Knit (V-shaped interlocking) stitch style", "Scale / Scale Mode: base stitch size and how it is chosen (Uniform, Variance, Min/Max)", "Jitter: random positional offset per stitch", "Angle: base rotation of every stitch in degrees", "Stretch X / Stretch Y: horizontal and vertical stretch per stitch", "Layer Mask parameters: strength with which each optional input affects the result"]

- Caveats: ["Leave transform controls at defaults for the Knit shape: moving individual stitches breaks interlocking fibers and creates discontinuities", "Layer Mask parameters have no effect unless the matching optional input is connected", "Purl-specific and Knit-specific controls apply only to their own shape type", "Round to Multiples is a post-process applied to the final stitch angle", "Page is labelled as available since Houdini 22.0"]

